module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.FpqcQuasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.QuasiCoherent.FpqcAffineOpenRefinement
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.QuasiCoherent.GaloisDescentEquivalence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.QuasiCoherent.ZariskiEssSurj
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Simplicial.DescentViaSimplicialSchemes
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Quasi-coherent modules along a morphism of schemes with a section

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a morphism of schemes admitting a section `σ`. The simplicial scheme
`(X/S)_•` of Stacks 024A has `X` in degree zero and `X ×_S X` in degree one, so a quasi-coherent
module on it is a quasi-coherent module `F` on `X` together with an isomorphism between the two
pullbacks of `F` to `X ×_S X` satisfying the cocycle condition — that is, a quasi-coherent
descent datum for the one-element family `{f}`. Pullback along `f` is an equivalence from the
quasi-coherent `O_S`-modules onto those data: the section provides a morphism of families in the
reverse direction, and restriction of descent data depends only on the induced morphism of
targets. The same conclusion holds under the weaker hypothesis of the source's footnote, that
`f` have a section fpqc locally on `S`, because the one-element family `{f}` then generates an
fpqc covering sieve and quasi-coherent modules are an fpqc stack.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentDescentData.pullFunctorIdIso`: restriction of quasi-coherent
  descent data along the identity morphism of a family is the identity functor.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.sectionFamilyHom`: a section of `f` read as a morphism from the one-element
  identity family of `S` to the one-element family `{f}`, over the identity of `S`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isEquivalence_pullFunctor_toTrivialFamily_of_section`: restriction along the
  morphism from `{f}` to the one-element identity family is an equivalence of quasi-coherent
  descent data as soon as `f` has a section.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isEquivalence_canonicalDescentFunctor_singleton_of_section` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.quasicoherentDescentEquivalenceOfSection`: **the equivalence of Stacks 07TL
  in its descent-data form.** Pullback along `f` is an equivalence from the quasi-coherent
  `O_S`-modules to the quasi-coherent descent data for `{f}`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.sieve_ofArrows_singleton_mem_fpqcTopology_of_fpqcLocalSection` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.quasicoherentDescentEquivalenceOfFpqcLocalSection`: **the same equivalence
  under the weaker hypothesis of the source's footnote**, that `f` admit a section fpqc locally
  on `S`. This is a genuine generalisation: a morphism with an fpqc-local section need not have
  a section.

## Implementation notes

The source states the lemma as an equivalence onto the quasi-coherent modules on
`((X/S)_•)_Zar`, and reduces it to the pairs `(F, α)` of Stacks 07TH. Those pairs are exactly
`AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentDescentData` for the one-element family `{f}`, which is the form
used here. The identification of the quasi-coherent modules on the total Zariski site of a
simplicial scheme with the cartesian pairs is Stacks 07TH and Stacks 0D7M. Stacks 07TH, the
equivalence between cartesian modules and pairs, is
`CategoryTheory.SimplicialSiteSituation.cartesianModuleSheafEquivCartesianModulePair` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Simplicial.ComponentRingedTopos.CartesianModulePairEquivalence`;
of Stacks 0D7M this development has only the right-hand side of the equivalence,
`CategoryTheory.SimplicialSiteSituation.IsCartesianWithQuasicoherentComponents` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Simplicial/ComponentRingedTopos/QuasicoherentCartesian.lean`,
neither direction of it being proved. Stacks 07TJ, which the source uses to know that a
pushforward is again quasi-coherent, is available for the components of the pushforward only,
`AlgebraicGeometry.SimplicialScheme.isQuasicoherent_componentModule_modulePushforward` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Simplicial/ZariskiPushforwardQuasicoherent.lean`.
The clause label on the tag records this.

The proof is the one the source gives, organised as in Stacks 0243 for descent data of schemes:
a section `σ` and the morphism `f` itself are mutually inverse morphisms of families over
`𝟙 S` up to the comparison
`AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentDescentData.pullFunctorIsoOfEq`, which says that restriction of
descent data depends only on the induced morphism of targets. The hypothesis is used nowhere
else; in particular no flatness or quasi-compactness enters, and the statement is universe
polymorphic in the scheme universe.

The footnote's form is proved separately and does not pass through the section form: an
fpqc-local section makes the sieve generated by `{f}` contain an fpqc covering family, so that
sieve is fpqc covering, and the fpqc stack property of quasi-coherent modules applies directly.
That route uses genuinely more input — the fpqc descent of Stacks 023S and 023T — which is why
both forms are kept.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07TL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07TL)
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe w v u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace QuasicoherentDescentData

/-- Restriction of quasi-coherent descent data along the identity morphism of a family is the
identity functor. This is the transfer to quasi-coherent components of
`CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData.pullFunctorIdIso`. -/
def pullFunctorIdIso {U : Scheme.{u}} (𝒰 : PreZeroHypercover.{w} U) :
    pullFunctor (PreZeroHypercover.HomOver.id 𝒰) ≅ 𝟭 (QuasicoherentDescentData 𝒰.f) := by
  let e := Pseudofunctor.DescentData.pullFunctorIdIso
    (F := modulePullbackPseudofunctor) (f := 𝒰.f) U
  let ι𝒰 := ObjectProperty.ι (fun D : modulePullbackPseudofunctor.DescentData 𝒰.f ↦
    ∀ i, (D.obj i).IsQuasicoherent)
  exact NatIso.ofComponents
    (fun D ↦ (ObjectProperty.isoMk
      (P := fun D : modulePullbackPseudofunctor.DescentData 𝒰.f ↦
        ∀ i, (D.obj i).IsQuasicoherent)
      (e.app (ι𝒰.obj D)) :
        (pullFunctor (PreZeroHypercover.HomOver.id 𝒰)).obj D ≅ D))
    fun φ ↦ ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (e.hom.naturality (ι𝒰.map φ))

end QuasicoherentDescentData

variable {X S : Scheme.{u}}

/-- A section `σ` of `f : X ⟶ S`, read as a morphism from the one-element identity family of `S`
to the one-element family `{f}`, lying over the identity of `S`. -/
def sectionFamilyHom (f : X ⟶ S) (σ : S ⟶ X) (hσ : σ ≫ f = 𝟙 S) :
    (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} (𝟙 S)).HomOver
      (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} f) (𝟙 S) where
  s₀ _ := PUnit.unit
  h₀ _ := σ
  w₀ _ := hσ.trans (Category.id_comp _).symm

/-- If `f : X ⟶ S` has a section, restriction of quasi-coherent descent data along the morphism
from the one-element family `{f}` to the one-element identity family of `S` is an equivalence. -/
theorem isEquivalence_pullFunctor_toTrivialFamily_of_section
    (f : X ⟶ S) (σ : S ⟶ X) (hσ : σ ≫ f = 𝟙 S) :
    (QuasicoherentDescentData.pullFunctor
      (toTrivialFamily (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} f))).IsEquivalence := by
  set Φ := toTrivialFamily (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} f)
  set Ψ := sectionFamilyHom f σ hσ
  have hk : (𝟙 S) ≫ (𝟙 S) = 𝟙 S := Category.comp_id _
  let η : 𝟭 (QuasicoherentDescentData (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} (𝟙 S)).f) ≅
      QuasicoherentDescentData.pullFunctor Φ ⋙ QuasicoherentDescentData.pullFunctor Ψ :=
    (QuasicoherentDescentData.pullFunctorIdIso _).symm ≪≫
      QuasicoherentDescentData.pullFunctorIsoOfEq (PreZeroHypercover.HomOver.id _)
        (Ψ.comp Φ hk) rfl ≪≫
      (QuasicoherentDescentData.pullFunctorCompIso Ψ Φ hk).symm
  let ε : QuasicoherentDescentData.pullFunctor Ψ ⋙ QuasicoherentDescentData.pullFunctor Φ ≅
      𝟭 (QuasicoherentDescentData (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} f).f) :=
    QuasicoherentDescentData.pullFunctorCompIso Φ Ψ hk ≪≫
      QuasicoherentDescentData.pullFunctorIsoOfEq (Φ.comp Ψ hk)
        (PreZeroHypercover.HomOver.id _) rfl ≪≫
      QuasicoherentDescentData.pullFunctorIdIso _
  exact (CategoryTheory.Equivalence.mk _ _ η ε).isEquivalence_functor

/-- The canonical descent functor of the one-element identity family of a scheme is an
equivalence: the family is a Zariski covering, so both halves of Stacks 023E apply. -/
theorem isEquivalence_canonicalDescentFunctor_identitySingleton (S : Scheme.{u}) :
    (canonicalDescentFunctor (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} (𝟙 S)).f).IsEquivalence := by
  have : ∀ i, IsOpenImmersion ((PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} (𝟙 S)).f i) :=
    fun _ ↦ inferInstanceAs (IsOpenImmersion (𝟙 S))
  have hcov : ⨆ i, Scheme.Hom.opensRange ((PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} (𝟙 S)).f i) = ⊤ := by
    change (⨆ _ : PUnit.{1}, Scheme.Hom.opensRange (𝟙 S)) = ⊤
    simp only [iSup_const]
    ext x
    simp
  exact Stacks.Descent.isEquivalence_canonicalDescentFunctor
    (Stacks.Descent.nonempty_fullyFaithful_canonicalDescentFunctor_zariski
      (f := (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} (𝟙 S)).f) hcov)
    (Stacks.Descent.isEffective_zariski
      (f := (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} (𝟙 S)).f) hcov)

/-- **Stacks 07TL, in its descent-data form.** If `f : X ⟶ S` has a section, the canonical
functor from quasi-coherent `O_S`-modules to the quasi-coherent descent data for the one-element
family `{f}` — equivalently, to the quasi-coherent modules on the simplicial scheme `(X/S)_•` —
is an equivalence of categories. -/
theorem isEquivalence_canonicalDescentFunctor_singleton_of_section
    (f : X ⟶ S) (σ : S ⟶ X) (hσ : σ ≫ f = 𝟙 S) :
    (canonicalDescentFunctor (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} f).f).IsEquivalence := by
  have := isEquivalence_canonicalDescentFunctor_identitySingleton S
  have := isEquivalence_pullFunctor_toTrivialFamily_of_section f σ hσ
  exact Functor.isEquivalence_of_iso
    (pullTrivialDescentIso (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} f))

/-- **Stacks 07TL, in its descent-data form.** For a morphism of schemes `f : X ⟶ S` with a
section, pullback is an equivalence between the category of quasi-coherent `O_S`-modules and the
category of quasi-coherent descent data for `{f}`, i.e. the quasi-coherent modules on the
simplicial scheme `(X/S)_•` of Stacks 024A. -/
@[stacks 07TL "the equivalence, with its target in descent-data form: the quasi-coherent \
descent data for {f}, not yet identified with QCoh(((X/S)_bullet)_Zar); that identification \
is the cited 07TJ together with 07TH, and 07TJ is absent here"]
def quasicoherentDescentEquivalenceOfSection
    (f : X ⟶ S) (σ : S ⟶ X) (hσ : σ ≫ f = 𝟙 S) :
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent S.ringCatSheaf).FullSubcategory ≌
      QuasicoherentDescentData (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} f).f :=
  have := isEquivalence_canonicalDescentFunctor_singleton_of_section f σ hσ
  (canonicalDescentFunctor (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} f).f).asEquivalence

/-- If a family generates an fpqc covering sieve, the canonical descent functor of Stacks 023D
is an equivalence: quasi-coherent modules are a stack for the fpqc topology. -/
theorem isEquivalence_canonicalDescentFunctor_of_sieve_mem_fpqcTopology
    {I : Type v} {Y : I → Scheme.{u}} {g : ∀ i, Y i ⟶ S}
    (hg : Sieve.ofArrows Y g ∈ Scheme.fpqcTopology.{u} S) :
    (canonicalDescentFunctor g).IsEquivalence :=
  Stacks.Descent.isEquivalence_canonicalDescentFunctor
    (Stacks.Descent.nonempty_fullyFaithful_canonicalDescentFunctor_of_isPrestack_of_sieve_mem hg)
    (Stacks.Descent.isEffective_of_isStack_of_sieve_mem hg)

/-- A morphism which admits a section fpqc locally on its target generates an fpqc covering
sieve on its own: every member of the fpqc covering family factors through it. -/
theorem sieve_ofArrows_singleton_mem_fpqcTopology_of_fpqcLocalSection
    (f : X ⟶ S) {I : Type v} {T : I → Scheme.{u}} (p : ∀ i, T i ⟶ S)
    (hp : Presieve.ofArrows T p ∈ Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.{u} S)
    (s : ∀ i, T i ⟶ X) (hs : ∀ i, s i ≫ f = p i) :
    Sieve.ofArrows (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} f).X
      (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} f).f ∈ Scheme.fpqcTopology.{u} S := by
  refine Scheme.fpqcTopology.superset_covering ?_ (Precoverage.generate_mem_toGrothendieck hp)
  rw [Sieve.generate_le_iff]
  rintro Z q ⟨i⟩
  exact ⟨X, s i, f, ⟨PUnit.unit⟩, hs i⟩

/-- **Stacks 07TL in the stronger form of its footnote, in the descent-data form.** If `f` admits
a section after an fpqc covering of `S`, pullback is an equivalence between the quasi-coherent
`O_S`-modules and the quasi-coherent descent data for `{f}`, i.e. the quasi-coherent modules on
the simplicial scheme `(X/S)_•` of Stacks 024A. -/
@[stacks 07TL "the footnote's stronger form, f having a section only fpqc locally on S; target \
in descent-data form as above, its identification with QCoh(((X/S)_bullet)_Zar) being the cited \
07TJ together with 07TH, and 07TJ is absent here"]
def quasicoherentDescentEquivalenceOfFpqcLocalSection
    (f : X ⟶ S) {I : Type v} {T : I → Scheme.{u}} (p : ∀ i, T i ⟶ S)
    (hp : Presieve.ofArrows T p ∈ Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.{u} S)
    (s : ∀ i, T i ⟶ X) (hs : ∀ i, s i ≫ f = p i) :
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent S.ringCatSheaf).FullSubcategory ≌
      QuasicoherentDescentData (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} f).f :=
  have := isEquivalence_canonicalDescentFunctor_of_sieve_mem_fpqcTopology
    (sieve_ofArrows_singleton_mem_fpqcTopology_of_fpqcLocalSection f p hp s hs)
  (canonicalDescentFunctor (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} f).f).asEquivalence

end AlgebraicGeometry

end

end
